      "created_at": "2015-02-23T03:58:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, I've decided to read the book. I'm only about six pages or so in, but I think I have enough info to start a drinking game.</p><p>Take a drink whenever:</p><p>Someone says that Kate is tenacious.</p><p>Ana&nbsp;says either to herself or outloud that&nbsp;Christian Gray&nbsp;is arrogant.</p><p>Finish your drink if Ana refers to Christain Gray as a control-freak.</p><p>Whenever the author uses a cliche without any sense of irony.</p><p>Whenever someone or something talks in a stern voice.</p><p>Whenever someone or something talks in a nice voice.</p><p>Take a shot whenever someone raises an eyebrow. Take an additional shot if an adverb is used to describe how the eyebrow was raised.</p><p>Optional rule: Take a shot whenever Ana remarks how handsome Christian Grey is. After 6 pages, you'll be wasted.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:56.576Z",
